  <DsSection id="tokens-feed" title="Token feed">
    <p>
      <a href={DS_BASE + "/tokens.json"}><code>GET /design-system/tokens.json</code></a> returns every <code>:root</code> token
      ({tokens.length} today) with its raw value, resolved literal, group and dark-mode value, plus the motion tokens, breakpoints and
      the long-list constants. It is generated from <code>global.css</code> at build time, so it cannot drift. Requires a signed-in
      session (or an agent bearer token per the <code>workos-agent-auth</code> skill), like every other route.
    </p>
    <div class="ds-pre"><code>&#123;
  "name": "Pro Exteriors Command Center",
  "version": "0.6.551A",
  "source": "app/command-center/src/styles/global.css :root",
  "modes": ["light", "dark"],
  "tokens": [
    &#123; "name": "--color-primary", "group": "color", "value": "#11133f", "resolved": "#11133f", "dark": null &#125;,
    &#123; "name": "--color-surface", "group": "color", "value": "#ffffff", "resolved": "#ffffff", "dark": "#161d27" &#125;,
    …
  ],
  "motion": &#123; "--motion-fast": "120ms", … &#125;,
  "breakpoints": &#123; "rail": 1180, "stack": 820, "toc": 1280 &#125;,
  "longList": &#123; "pageSize": 10, "control": "Show all N … ▾ (M more)" &#125;
&#125;</code></div>
    <p>An agent reads the feed once per session, then uses token names in CSS. It never writes a resolved hex into a component.</p>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="escalation" title="When to escalate">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Do</th><th>Never</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>A needed value is not a token</td><td>Add it to <code>:root</code> deliberately, document it in the relevant chapter, cite the reason</td><td>Inline it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>A brand colour's role would change</td><td>Escalate to the account manager (DSN-011); do not proceed</td><td>Swap it locally</td></tr>
          <tr><td>A surface wants monospace</td><td>Escalate the product question: is this a Property Card?</td><td>Grant mono inline</td></tr>
          <tr><td>A user request conflicts with a rule here</td><td>Explain the rule and its evidence once; if the request is repeated, do it and add a decisions-log row with the evidence</td><td>Quietly diverge; quietly refuse</td></tr>
          <tr><td>A figure's meaning would change (basis, denominator)</td><td>Flag it as a doctrine change before shipping (D-09)</td><td>Ship it silently</td></tr>
          <tr><td>A new motion, breakpoint, page shape or component</td><td>Add the rule and specimen here in the same PR</td><td>Ship it undocumented</td></tr>
          <tr><td>This site and a screen disagree</td><td>Fix the source (<code>global.css</code> or the surface) and this site together</td><td>Patch a screenshot; edit a copy</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The client supplies new logo artwork</td><td>Replace the stand-ins in <code>config/brand/assets/</code>, re-render swag, update the Logo chapter</td><td>Keep both</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="G-01" title="Every PR that touches a surface cites the rule ids it applied and any it broke, with the user evidence for the break." source="Overview G-00">
        <p>The checklist above is the template.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="G-02" title="A surface is not done until it was opened in a browser in both modes and at 390px; build and tests green are necessary, not sufficient." source="docs/100:36-50; CLAUDE.md 'verify the live call path'">
        <p>Two shipped regressions passed build and tests.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="G-03" title="Deploys are explain-then-ship: state the change, the user-visible impact and the rollback, then push and watch /healthz." source="CLAUDE.md Live ⇄ Dev alignment">
        <p>The agent deploys; the human reads.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="G-04" title="This site is the design source of truth and is updated in the same PR as the change it describes." source="CONVENTIONS §11; this chapter">
        <p>Design.md and standards/design/v1.md are updated when a principle or a pass/fail check changes.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="G-05" title="Rule ids are permanent; retire with a note, never renumber; new rules append." source="Overview → Rule index">
        <p>Other docs, PRs and issues link to them.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

